### Build from source

{% if ros2_package_manager == 'pixi' %}
Everything — ROS and dev tooling — is managed by pixi:

```sh
pixi install                 # create the ROS environment (conda-forge)
pixi run colcon build --symlink-install --packages-select {{ package_name }}
pixi run colcon test --packages-select {{ package_name }}
pixi run colcon test-result --verbose
```
{% else %}
The ROS environment comes from apt; the pure-Python dev tooling
(ruff/pytest/pre-commit) is managed by {{ package_manager }}:

```sh
# Install build tools (once per machine)
sudo apt install python3-colcon-common-extensions python3-rosdep
sudo rosdep init && rosdep update

# Install the dev tooling (ruff, pytest, pre-commit, ...)
{% if package_manager == "uv" %}uv sync
{% elif package_manager == "poetry" %}poetry install
{% endif %}
# Build this package
rosdep install --from-paths . --ignore-src -r -y
colcon build --symlink-install --packages-select {{ package_name }}
source install/setup.bash
```
{% endif %}

